  "body": "## What changed\n\nCargo 1.100 puts each workspace unit in its own directory, `target/<profile>/build/<package>/<hash>/`. The hash covers the profile of the unit. Agents ran gates in the shared build worktree with `CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0` and with the default (incremental on). `CARGO_INCREMENTAL` sets `profile.incremental`. Thus each run with the other value gave all of about 600 `camcraft-app` units a new directory (about 190 MB each). Cargo does not remove the old directories.\n\n- New `xtask/src/unit_env.rs`: each cargo call of a gate gets `CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0`. The gate removes the caller's `CARGO_PROFILE_*` and `CARGO_BUILD_INCREMENTAL` variables.\n- `direct::cargo` (the one place where a gate step starts cargo) and the three catalog cargo calls apply the pin.\n- At the start, the gate prints the pin, each removed variable, and a note when `RUSTFLAGS` / `CARGO_ENCODED_RUSTFLAGS` / `CARGO_BUILD_RUSTFLAGS` is set.\n- The summary prints the number of unit directories that the run added.\n- The `gate` skill tells about the pin. `docs/decisions/3150-gate-unit-env.md` records the cause and the choice (incremental off, because sccache cannot cache incremental units and the disk is the defect).\n\n## Readings (shared build worktree issue-917, 2026-11-21)\n\n- The manifests, `Cargo.lock` and `.cargo/config.toml` were the same at the last six gated heads. But the `profile` fingerprint hash of one test unit had 3 values over 5 runs. Third-party units did not change.\n- After the fix, `cargo xtask gate test flat_volume_has_finite_width_depth_and_segment_ends --crate cl` ran two times: caller `CARGO_INCREMENTAL` unset gave `unit directories: 5152, none added`; caller `CARGO_INCREMENTAL=1` gave `unit directories: 5152, none added`.\n- A plain `CARGO_INCREMENTAL=1 cargo test -p camcraft-cl --no-run` selected the other unit hash of `camcraft-kernel` (`573773ead6d4af3d`, an incremental variant). This confirms the cause.\n\n## Pinning tests (`cargo test -p xtask`: 240 passed)\n\n- `unit_env::tests::every_gate_cargo_call_gets_the_same_unit_env`\n- `unit_env::tests::direct_cargo_steps_apply_the_unit_env`\n- `unit_env::tests::batch_steps_share_the_flags_that_enter_the_unit_hash`\n- `unit_env::tests::profile_variables_are_removed_and_others_kept`\n- `unit_env::tests::notes_name_the_pin_and_each_removed_or_noted_variable`\n- `unit_env::tests::units_count_nested_unit_directories_only`\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- A full quick or batch gate two times on the same tree. The probe used one `gate test` step.\n- The old unit directories are not removed. The first gate run after the merge can add one more `CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0` variant where none is present. The decision file says why there is no prune.\n- No heavy lane: the diff touches only `xtask/`, `.claude/skills/gate/` and `docs/decisions/`.\n\nProcess change: yes\n\nEffort: high\n\nChangelog: none\n\nFixes #3150\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
